'/scratch/kohlbach/gate-in-1.12/PXD006096/100815_MM_ABPP_H1993_DMSO_DIA1_new.mzML' is raw DIA: the precursor m/z of its MS2 repeats in a cycle of 126 isolation windows (median 8 Th, 451-1333 m/z, periodicity 1, 100% uncharged). Each MS2 mixes several peptides and its 'precursor' is a window, so tags would get wrong flanking masses and complement statistics. Generate pseudo-DDA spectra first, e.g. DIAspeXtract -in /scratch/kohlbach/gate-in-1.12/PXD006096/100815_MM_ABPP_H1993_DMSO_DIA1_new.mzML -out /scratch/kohlbach/gate-in-1.12/PXD006096/100815_MM_ABPP_H1993_DMSO_DIA1_new.pseudo.mzML (diaTracer also works for .d), then run FASTag on that file. To tag the raw DIA spectra anyway (experts; flanks and complements will be wrong), add -acquisition_check warn.
